{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF04", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: four records on live suppression-trigger timing in playoff replays (101 to 228 triggers). Triggers were 100% actionable; BEST vs AVOID was p=0.073965 in the 10-series replay and confirmed in the 25-series replay. The early-vs-late gap (0.701 vs 0.415) rests on 26 early triggers, and one record calls its p=0.031 (n=57) weak evidence. Applies to timing claims drawn from small early-trigger subsets.", "document": "# FAM:SF04 | Study family SF04: Live trigger timing: early vs late detection\n- observed_research_question: Live trigger timing: early vs late detection\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Earlier suppression triggers leave time to act and yield better BEST-counter outcomes.\n- observed_result: [APPM-028] Tier Spearman rho -0.2066 p=1e-06 n=557; BEST-AVOID gap early 0.701 (26 triggers) vs late 0.415 (202); rho 0.2859 p=0.031 n=57.\n- observed_result: [APPS-028] 101 triggers; 100% actionable (>=5 H2 poss remaining); mean remaining 23.4. Spearman tier vs ROG PPP rho=-0.0457, p=0.45616, n=268. MW BEST 1.227 (n=30) vs AVOID 1.037 (n=95), p=0.073965 (not confirmed at 0.05 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [APPS-029] 228 triggers, 100% actionable, mean remaining 21.0. Spearman rho=-0.2066, p=1e-06, n=557. MW BEST 1.263 (n=57) vs AVOID 0.783 (n=110), p=0.0. Early BEST-AVOID gap 0.701 vs late 0.415.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_confidence: low (0.26)"}, {"id": "FAM:SF20", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: pre-registered test on 23 player-season absences from 18 franchises. V1 (structure moves under real absence) was confirmed; V2 (the simulation predicts the magnitude) was not (rho +0.288, CI -0.244 to +0.667), with franchises below the registered floor of about 20. Applies to magnitude tests on this absence pool. One record notes that a later full-pool run reversed V2.", "document": "# FAM:SF20 | Study family SF20: Absence validation (structure moves under real absence; simulation tracks it)\n- observed_research_question: Absence validation (structure moves under real absence; simulation tracks it)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Real player absences move the association structure (V1) and the LOO simulation predicts the magnitude (V2).\n- observed_result: [APPA-006] Gate G2 21/23 (91%) above null median; V1(a) 16/23 above own-null p95, binomial p=2.67e-16; V1(b) mean(D_real - median_null)=+0.142, CI [+0.103, +0.187].\n- observed_result: [APPA-007] Gate G3 Spearman +0.099. V2a Spearman +0.288, p=0.077, CI [-0.244, +0.667] FAIL; V2b partial +0.253, p=0.115, CI [-0.262, +0.615] FAIL. Diagnostics: H_code ruled out (rho=0.933); dropping 2 absorption cases rh [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [PAP-023] V1(a) 16/23 above p95 binomial p=2.67e-16; V1(b) +0.142 CI[+0.103,+0.187] CONFIRMED; V2a rho=+0.288 p=0.077 CI[-0.244,+0.667]; V2b rho=+0.253 p=0.115 NOT\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-009", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: compared V4 and V5 player routing on observed PPP. There were 8 divergences and none was scoreable: players were missing from Neo4j and V5 mostly routed to 'team'. Applies to routing comparisons that need player-level PPP from the graph; the record notes data coverage could be checked before running. No hit rate was recorded.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-009 | Study family SF-APPS-009: Player routing V4 vs V5 direct scoring\n- observed_research_question: Player routing V4 vs V5 direct scoring\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: V5 player routing picks players with higher observed PPP than V4 routing.\n- observed_result: 8 divergences, 0 scoreable, 8 unscored (player missing from Neo4j); hit rate n/a.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Scoreable 0 of 8; V5 mostly routed to 'team' rather than a player.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=8 divergences, 0 scoreable\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Series where V4 and V5 routed to different players; compare observed PPP (n>=5 each).\n- observed_verdict: inconclusive\n- observed_failure_type: A_unanswerable\n- auto_confidence: high (0.95)"}, {"id": "FAM:SF31", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: scanned 6,221 (offense, opponent, play type) cells for head-to-head leaders who differ from the season default. The apparent edge (+1.26 PPP at n>=5, +1.13 at n>=15) came from low-n cells, for example 1-shot role players at 3.00 PPP. Applies to routing or matchup signals estimated from cells with few possessions. The records recommend keeping the n>=15 gate.", "document": "# FAM:SF31 | Study family SF31: Routing prior vs H2H posterior gate diagnostic\n- observed_research_question: Routing prior vs H2H posterior gate diagnostic\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The n>=15 H2H gate suppresses real player-routing signal.\n- observed_result: [APPM-015] Mean PPP delta lead-default +1.259 (n>=5) to +1.129 (n>=15); low-n leaders are role players with 2-3 PPP on 5-7 possessions.\n- observed_result: [CHT-017] At n=5-9 typical leaders are 1-shot 3.00-PPP role players. Mean PPP delta lead-vs-default +1.26 at n>=5 and +1.13 at n>=15, inflated by small-sample distortion. n>=15 routing-override gate judged to filter nois [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: [APPM-015] Apparent +1.13 PPP edge is small-sample inflation (e.g. n=6, PPP=3.00).\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
